data bin_witness_wet_per_row_wall_budget_seconds: Int = 60

data bin_witness_wet_per_row_budget_note: String = "Short/quick-witness discipline for the per-PR wet batch (CI floor endgame D6, operator ruling 2026-07-23): per-PR CI is short/quick witnesses, and a bin-execution row's subprocess wall is invisible to the fast-lane 5-second EVAL deadline by construction (the deadline counts interpreter CPU; child-process wall is host-effect time), so the bin lane carries its own per-row wall budget — this datum. A row whose MEASURED wall exceeds it re-homes to the falsifier wet cadence as a typed frontier row (falsifier_rehomed_bin_wet_rows below, reason + dissolve_on per row), keeping the remaining rows as the per-PR smoke subset so plumbing-diff PRs retain a discriminating signal. Classification basis: run 30009199696's per-row cost table (the 54-row pool's 561s eval was 94 percent three rows: floor_skip_discovery 289s, cross_shard_seam live-tree 183s, dag_compile_clean_perturb 53s — the third is under budget and stays). Enforcement layering: this datum is the classification rule applied at review; the EXECUTABLE wall against silent regrowth is the batch clamp (gunbc.ci_spec gunbc_ci_floor_batch_clamp_params — a new heavy row grows the wet batch's unit count and can blow its derived clamp, reding with a typed refusal), so an over-budget enrollment cannot ride silently even if review misses it."

type RehomedBinWetRow {
  entry: String
  function: String
  reason: String
  dissolve_on: String
}

data falsifier_rehomed_bin_wet_rows: List<RehomedBinWetRow> = [
  RehomedBinWetRow {
    entry: "dag/test/claim/floor_skip_discovery_witness_test.dag",
    function: "floor_skip_discovery_keystone_holds",
    reason: "289s measured on run 30009199696 (4.8x the per-row budget), AND a per-PR duplicate: the row runs the floor_skip_discovery_witness binary that the ci job's own Affected-set selection control step already runs on every PR — the per-PR widen-detector coverage is the step, so the row's per-PR seat bought a second copy of the same suite",
    dissolve_on: "the selection-control suite's shared-index rework lands the binary under bin_witness_wet_per_row_wall_budget_seconds on a measured run — then either re-enroll per-PR consciously or delete this row as a duplicate of the step (whichever the measured wall admits)"
  },
  RehomedBinWetRow {
    entry: "dag/test/claim/dag_compile_clean_seam_witness_test.dag",
    function: "cross_shard_seam_preservation_holds_on_live_tree",
    reason: "183s measured on run 30009199696 (3x the per-row budget): the live-tree seam-preservation leg compiles real cross-shard closures per seam; its cheap algebra sibling (cross_shard_seam_algebra_holds) stays per-PR as the smoke row for the concern",
    dissolve_on: "seam preservation gains a scoped or receipt-consuming realization measured under the per-row budget; then re-enroll per-PR and delete this row"
  }
]

fn falsifier_rehomed_bin_wet_entries() -> List<ScheduleWitnessEntry> {
  fold(falsifier_rehomed_bin_wet_rows, init: [], f: fn(acc, r) {
    concat(acc, [bin_wet(entry: r.entry, f: r.function)])
  })
}

data falsifier_silent_pick_gate_note: String = "Nightly falsifier batch 4 (#6967 consumption, 2026-07-21; #7013 fast-follow hardening 2026-07-22): the SilentPickTelemetry the legacy resolver emits at v1_rt.rs (recorded at src/v1/04_env.dag global_bare LCP pick+tie and src/v1/04_sigs.dag fn-parent first-hit) had zero consumers — a live DESIGN §5 fail-open, since §13 (unique-on-chain resolution, operator-ratified 2026-07-21) rejects every silent-pick arm as a class. This roster runs resolution_divergence_census --closure-scoped (compile-clean closure authority via witness_layer_roots + load_compile_clean_entry_sources, not a blind whole-tree walk) as a bin-execution witness: it enables the telemetry, drains it, and refuses fail-closed in two arms before exit 0 — (1) resolution_divergence_fn_parent_first_hit_subset_refusal: construction invariant that every in-roster fn_parent_first_hit fire is containment_ambiguous (v2.test.* intentional-ambiguity harness modules excluded via resolution_divergence_census_roster_excluded_module_prefixes, green-by-execution witness resolution_divergence_fn_parent_first_hit_subset_holds_on_closure_scoped_corpus), then (2) resolution_divergence_silent_pick_refusal (single join authority shared with the binary exit code) on any GENUINE silent-pick — silent_pick_global_bare_lcp_rows, silent_pick_global_bare_lcp_tie_rows, and silent_pick_fn_parent_first_hit_rows joined against containment_ambiguous_rows/diverge_rows via resolution_divergence_silent_pick_genuine_rows, never the raw telemetry count (whole-pool name overlap alone over-fires benign on ~487 corpus sites; the join is the durable condition, review 41032). Refusals are SILENT-PICK-GATE-tagged stdout/stderr — a stable greppable marker chosen because the falsifier's other batches are red for unrelated reasons and an undifferentiated job-conclusion flip would be invisible. Baseline is 0 genuine rows (#6936's Diverge=0), never a tuned threshold — any nonzero genuine row is a fresh regression. `gunbc compile`'s own inline gate (main.rs) is a DIFFERENT, narrower, cost-motivated proxy — not this shared authority: it checks fn_parent_first_hits raw-count only (red-on-any, over-strict direction — safe if wrong) resting on the same construction-proven invariant above (roster exclusion applies at nightly cadence only, not in the compile-path proxy — v2.test.* modules stay outside today's compile-path census universe via /test/ path exclusion) and skips global_bare_lcp entirely (under-strict direction — a genuine global_bare_lcp pick is caught only by the nightly join-filtered falsifier backstop, not at compile time). The compile-path proxy and nightly falsifier remain asymmetric by design (cost), not a single authority today. A whole-tree Wet resolve cannot live on the per-PR affected-set floor (measured: still running past 90s / 3GB+ RSS on a cold run), so this rides the cold nightly whole-corpus control alongside falsifier_self_host_wet_entries and known_red_probe_entries, never the hermetic per-PR discovery corpus. This gate's live paging value is coupled to the falsifier itself being green and alerted on — both separate, unassigned ledger items as of this note; see the falsifier fallout audit. Dissolve-on: §13's unique-on-chain resolution ships as the resolver's actual behavior (no fallback arm to silently pick in the first place) — then telemetry, this witness, and this note all delete together."

data falsifier_silent_pick_gate_entries: List<ScheduleWitnessEntry> = [
  bin_wet(entry: "dag/test/claim/resolution_divergence_silent_pick_gate_witness_test.dag", f: "resolution_divergence_silent_pick_gate_keystone_holds")
]

data floor_skip_control_fixture_exclusion_note: String = "test/fixture/floor_skip/ is excluded from tree-wide discovery at DIR grain (parent ruling 2026-07-11: a fixture that WANTS witness enrollment is mis-homed by definition, and file-grain exclusion invites the next control fixture to repeat the landmine). These fixtures exist to be driven by floor_skip_discovery_witness's explicit rosters, not as corpus witnesses: falsifier_divergence_control_test.dag carries a BY-DESIGN red row (falsifier_red_control_holds returns false to prove the divergence attribution channel), so any completed full-corpus run - the nightly falsifier, or a PR whose diff touches its import closure - would red on a row whose red is the control's specification, and a permanent by-design divergence would also make the falsifier's 8-clean-window retirement criterion unsatisfiable; live_tree_declared_test.dag declares ReadsLiveTree as a control, so as a corpus row it would be a permanent never-skip cost with no enforcement value. Genuine corpus witnesses that were mis-homed here have been re-homed under test/claim/ (provenance_fail_closed_contract_test, live_tree_collision_test). Explicit-roster runs (the floor_skip bin) are unaffected: witness exclusions apply to discovery only."

data enforcement_coverage_exclusion_note: String = "The three enforcement coverage witnesses (enforcement/cost_coverage_witness_test.dag, enforcement/grammar_coverage_witness_test.dag, enforcement_live_witness_test.dag) are operator-ruled OFFLINE (2026-07-11). Receipt: their *_live fns read the corpus as data (live-tree rosters), so the PR-A never-predict-skip rule for live-tree rows made them run on EVERY wide PR regardless of diff; the block cost 22.0 min (main run 29137081535, busy fleet) and 21.0 min (PR run 29142398465, quiet fleet) of the 60-minute floor budget - about 35 percent - and their allocation ramp feeds the ~15GiB slot memory.high throttle that turns the floor tail into swap-speed work. Their input is corpus-denominated (the InputEnvelope axis, not layer span): per-PR admission wants a declared bounded envelope, which these rows cannot declare today. Offlining required TWO edits (cursor review catch, same PR): the discovery exclusion rows here AND removing the explicit CommitCheckEnrollment for enforcement_live_witness_test.dag in gunbc.commit_workflow - explicit roster rows merge after discovery with no exclusion filter (cli_run.rs explicit_entries dedup), and that is correct: an explicitly declared row should run, so offlining one means deleting its declaration, never teaching exclusions to veto the roster (a second authority). Run them via the local recipe: claim_batch --source-root dag --source-root src/v2 --entry <entry> per fn (all pure reads, no --wet needed). Dissolve-on: witness rows declare InputEnvelope/CostEnvelope and the scheduled (nightly) lane admits corpus-input rows under its own budget - then re-enroll consciously through the floor owner's lane; the affected-set-falsifier cadence covers interim drift."

data accumulator_copy_roster_gate_exclusion_note: String = "The three accumulator_copy_roster_gate*_test.dag witnesses are operator-ruled OFFLINE (2026-07-10: the gate is ~15m of serial interpreted resolve; run it via the claim_batch recipe in v2.lens.complexity_accumulator_copy.roster_gate). Excluded from discovery because the flip's selection cannot see them honestly either way: file_gate reads its roster targets via filesystem_read at runtime — a data dependency invisible to resolve-closure attribution — and the live-scan classifier reads only entry-file text, so the rows would be intermittently selected by lens/std-closure PRs (cost, against the ruling) while never firing on roster-target-only PRs (no enforcement). Dissolve-on: resolved-graph memoization receipts land AND G2 path-intersection (not G1 module-closure alone) is wired into floor admission axis (iv); then re-enroll consciously through the floor owner's lane."

data identity_captured_navigation_roster_gate_exclusion_note: String = "src/v2/test/claim/identity_captured_navigation/roster_gate_test.dag is operator-ruled OFFLINE for the identical structural reason as accumulator_copy_roster_gate_exclusion_note (2026-07-14): its corpus-sweep test fns call file_gate, which reads its roster targets (src/v2/extdeps/languages/dag.dag and siblings) via filesystem_read at runtime — a data dependency invisible to resolve-closure attribution — so per-PR selection would fire intermittently on lens/std-closure PRs (cost, against the ruling) while never firing on roster-target-only PRs (no enforcement). Run via the local recipe in v2.lens.identity_captured_navigation.roster_gate. Dissolve-on: identical to accumulator_copy_roster_gate — resolved-graph memoization receipts land AND G2 path-intersection is wired into floor admission axis (iv); then re-enroll consciously through the floor owner's lane."

data lever_a_local_receipt_witness_exclusion_note: String = "dag/test/claim/lever_a_local_receipt_witness_test.dag is operator-ruled OFFLINE (2026-07-11: witness_touched_path_dispositions_hold cold-scans compile_clean_shard_entry_paths via module_declaration_facts once per scoped disposition row — O(rows) full dag entry-tree walks, 85m+ CI timeout / OOM when selection runs it after lens_verdict on cli_run.dag PRs). LOCAL RECIPE (the whole of it — this row is the authority, no script file to maintain): claim_batch --source-root dag --source-root src/v2 --entry dag/test/claim/lever_a_local_receipt_witness_test.dag --function lever_a_local_receipts_hold --claim-run --wet. It formerly lived in scripts/lever_a_local_verify.sh, a pure sequencer around exactly that argv, deleted 2026-07-23 with the rest of scripts/ (operator ruling: a recipe is a command, not a file). Excluded from discovery for the same structural reason as accumulator_copy_roster_gate: the scoped rows read the shard roster at runtime — invisible to import-closure attribution — so skip-before-resolve cannot honestly bound cost. Dissolve-on: single-roster memo in tools.dag_compile_clean_scope lands AND G2 path-intersection (not G1 module-closure alone) is wired into floor admission axis (iv); then re-enroll through the floor owner's lane."

data whole_tree_strict_resolve_scaffold_exclusion_note: String = "The per-file rows below (everything after the three blanket prefixes and the two lens/application rows) are the strict-resolve-broken set, baked as single authority per operator ruling 2026-07-13 ('just make it single authority') — previously re-derived per probe run as --exclude-subpath args (M0/M1a receipts, docs/plans/v1-run-stability-throughline.md), a parallel representation this bake dissolves. Audited file-by-file 2026-07-13 (24 files, 5-group sweep with per-file execution receipts): 7 genuinely dead scaffolds were DELETED with their rows (the four Wave-A rung evals, the A.1.5a inprocess_equivalence one-shot, manual_corpus_eval, lens/idempotency/subject_roster — none witness-enrolled, zero importers, absent from the 1,776-witness cold corpus run); every row remaining guards a LIVE file — floor-discovered witnesses or their roster/receipt/lens dependencies, proven green by execution (the lens/testgen/ trio's four test-data witnesses PASS in the cold corpus run, overturning an initial dead-scaffold read). Their strict-resolve reds are universe-relative artifacts, NOT tree rot: each imports modules that EXIST in-tree (v2.test.manual.eval_runtime, v2.test.manual.connective_anchors, test fixtures) but sit behind this list's own blanket '/test/' and 'test/fixture/' rows, so the probe universe drops the import target while keeping the importer. Consumers are probe/instrument/census class only (measure_whole_tree_resolve, capture_func_env_semantic_oracle, wiring_liveness_whole_tree, measure_dependency_view_build, fn_arrow_decl_substrate census) — no witness-discovery or CI-gate coverage narrows. Dissolve each row on: its file relocates under a /test/ path (leaving the probe universe together with its import targets) or the blanket /test/ exclusion policy changes so its resolve repairs; a row that excludes nothing is dead weight, delete it. First relocation receipt (2026-07-14): the spice pair (spice_rc_passive_deck_claims_test, spice_rc_ngspice_oracle_test) re-homed to src/v2/test/claim/extdeps/ — they leave the probe universe with their fixtures, stay witness-discovered, and their two rows deleted per this trigger."

data resolution_divergence_census_roster_excluded_module_prefixes: List<String> = [
